---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy | 3D Tesla Roadster Game" 
  description="Read the Privacy Policy for the 3D Tesla Roadster Game. Learn how we safeguard user privacy, handle local browser storage for game saves, and maintain a safe WebGL experience."
  canonical="https://roadster-play.vercel.app/privacy"
  keywords="Privacy Policy Tesla Roadster Game, WebGL privacy, game data storage, cookie policy, GDPR compliance, player privacy, local storage simulator"
>
  <!-- Schema.org Structured Data: WebPage & BreadcrumbList -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "name": "Privacy Policy - 3D Tesla Roadster Game",
    "url": "https://roadster-play.vercel.app/privacy",
    "description": "Privacy policy and data transparency statement for the 3D Tesla Roadster Game driving simulator.",
    "breadcrumb": {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "https://roadster-play.vercel.app/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "Privacy Policy",
          "item": "https://roadster-play.vercel.app/privacy"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  </script>

  <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;">
    
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation -->
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <ol style="list-style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 13px; color: var(--mute); padding: 0; margin: 0; font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;">
        <li><a href="/" class="nav-link" style="padding: 0;">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--faint);">/</li>
        <li aria-current="page" style="color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600;">Privacy Policy</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Page Header / Hero -->
    <header style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
      <span class="mono-eyebrow" style="color: var(--link);">LEGAL &amp; DATA PRIVACY</span>
      <h1 class="display-xl" style="margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--ink);">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; color: var(--mute); font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;">
        EFFECTIVE DATE: OCTOBER 2026 &nbsp;•&nbsp; LAST REVISED: OCTOBER 29, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Key Privacy Highlights Banner -->
    <section class="vercel-card" style="padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; background: var(--canvas-elevated);">
      <span class="mono-eyebrow" style="color: var(--ink);">AT A GLANCE SUMMARY</span>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <div>
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Zero Personal Accounts</div>
          <p class="body-sm" style="color: var(--body);">No registration, email entry, password creation, or credit card requirements to play.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">100% Client-Side GPU</div>
          <p class="body-sm" style="color: var(--body);">All 3D WebGL rendering, shaders, and vehicle physics calculate strictly on your device.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">No Ad Broker Tracking</div>
          <p class="body-sm" style="color: var(--body);">We do not sell, rent, license, or monetize your personal information to third-party data brokers.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Local Browser Storage</div>
          <p class="body-sm" style="color: var(--body);">Lap records and theme settings are saved locally in your browser's localStorage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Detailed Policy Sections -->
    <article style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem; color: var(--body); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px;">
      
      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">1. Introduction &amp; Scope</h2>
        <p>
          Welcome to the <strong>3D Tesla Roadster Game</strong> ("we," "our," or "the simulator"), accessible via <a href="https://roadster-play.vercel.app/" class="nav-link" style="padding: 0; color: var(--link); text-decoration: underline;">https://roadster-play.vercel.app/</a> and all associated sub-routes. We are dedicated to maintaining the highest standard of digital transparency, user autonomy, and personal privacy.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          This Privacy Policy explains the nature of information processed when you visit our website, run the interactive WebGL driving simulation, or communicate with our development team.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">2. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike conventional digital game services, our website is architected from the ground up to respect user anonymity. Specifically:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;">
          <li>We <strong>do not require</strong> user accounts, logins, passwords, or profile credentials.</li>
          <li>We <strong>do not collect</strong> real names, physical postal addresses, telephone numbers, or financial payment details.</li>
          <li>We <strong>do not access</strong> device microphones, cameras, contacts, or local file systems.</li>
          <li>We <strong>do not track</strong> precise GPS location coordinates.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">3. Client-Side Browser Storage (`localStorage`)</h2>
        <p>
          To enhance your user experience, retain your visual theme preference, and persist in-game achievements, our application utilizes standard HTML5 Web Storage (<code style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; background: var(--canvas-sunken); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--hairline);">localStorage</code>) stored locally on your device:
        </p>
        <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 6px;">
          <table class="specs-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Key Name</th>
                <th>Storage Scope</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;">roadster-theme</td>
                <td>Client Device Only</td>
                <td>Remembers your preference between Light Mode and Dark Mode across page reloads.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;">roadster-records</td>
                <td>Client Device Only</td>
                <td>Stores your personal best 0–60 MPH times and 1/4 mile drag strip elapsed times.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;">roadster-audio-mute</td>
                <td>Client Device Only</td>
                <td>Remembers whether in-engine synthesizer audio effects are enabled or muted.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.85rem; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--mute);">
          <em>Notice:</em> None of this data is transmitted to or stored on external servers. You can clear this data at any time by clearing your browser cache or site data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">4. WebGL Execution &amp; Hardware Diagnostics</h2>
        <p>
          The 3D Tesla Roadster Game runs entirely within your browser's WebGL / Canvas context using Three.js. 
          The simulation queries your browser's WebGL capability strings (such as supported texture sizes and floating-point shader precision) solely to configure appropriate render settings. 
          These capability queries are processed dynamically in local memory during runtime and are never aggregated into persistent fingerprinting profiles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">5. Server Access Logs &amp; Edge Delivery</h2>
        <p>
          When you request pages, scripts, or 3D assets (<code style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px;">.glb</code> files), our global content delivery network (CDN) edge infrastructure automatically records standard technical access log entries. These logs may contain:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;">
          <li>Internet Protocol (IP) address (used for geographic edge routing and anti-DDoS defense)</li>
          <li>Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) requested</li>
          <li>HTTP user-agent string (browser brand and operating system version)</li>
          <li>Date and millisecond timestamp of the HTTP request</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          Server access logs are retained strictly for network diagnostic uptime monitoring, edge security mitigation, and bot traffic mitigation, after which they are automatically rotated and purged in compliance with industry security protocols.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">6. Third-Party CDNs &amp; Resources</h2>
        <p>
          To maintain sub-second loading performance and visual consistency across all operating systems, our site loads typography from Google Fonts (<code style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px;">Geist</code> and <code style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px;">Inter</code>) and script libraries from vetted public CDNs (such as cdnjs). Requests to these content delivery networks are governed by the respective providers' security and privacy policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">7. Analytics &amp; Performance Metrics</h2>
        <p>
          We employ Google Analytics (Google tag: <code style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px;">G-L9VFLEVQ68</code>) to gather aggregate, non-personally identifiable diagnostic insights such as page visits, device operating systems, WebGL capability support, and session stability. This data is utilized strictly to optimize simulator frame rates, diagnose graphics rendering across diverse GPUs, and improve user experience.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          We do <strong>not</strong> sell, rent, or trade visitor data to marketing brokers, nor do we run third-party advertising tracking networks or intrusive cross-site fingerprinting scripts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">8. Children’s Privacy (COPPA &amp; GDPR-K)</h2>
        <p>
          Our WebGL hypercar simulator is designed for general audiences and automotive technology enthusiasts. Because we do not collect personal identifying information from any user, we do not knowingly solicit or collect personal information from children under the age of 13 (or under 16 within the European Economic Area), in compliance with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and GDPR Article 8.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 9 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">9. Your Privacy Rights (GDPR &amp; CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
        <p>
          Under international privacy frameworks including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA), visitors possess legal rights concerning their data:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;">
          <li><strong>Right to Know &amp; Access:</strong> You have the right to know what data is collected (as detailed in this document).</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Deletion:</strong> Because all user records (high scores, themes) reside in your browser's local storage, you hold unilateral power to delete all records instantly by clearing site data.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We provide identical high-fidelity WebGL simulation access to all visitors regardless of privacy choices.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 10 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">10. How to Clear Stored Game Data</h2>
        <p>
          If you wish to remove all locally stored game benchmarks, lap times, or theme records from your browser:
        </p>
        <ol style="margin-top: 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;">
          <li>Open your browser settings (Chrome: <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+Del</kbd> or Safari: Preferences &gt; Privacy).</li>
          <li>Select <strong>Clear Browsing Data</strong> and choose <strong>Cookies and other site data</strong>.</li>
          <li>Alternatively, open Developer Tools (<kbd>F12</kbd>), navigate to the <em>Application</em> tab, expand <em>Local Storage</em>, and click <em>Clear All</em>.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 11 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">11. Modifications to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may periodically update this Privacy Policy to reflect enhancements in the simulator engine, new gameplay features, or updates in legal statutes. Any modifications will be indicated by the "Last Revised" date at the top of this document. Continued use of the website constitutes acceptance of any revised terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 12 -->
      <section style="border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding-top: 2rem;">
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">12. Contacting the Team</h2>
        <p>
          If you have inquiries, questions regarding data transparency, or technical observations regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact our team:
        </p>
        <div style="margin-top: 1rem;">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-pill-primary" style="height: 38px; padding: 0 18px; font-size: 13px;">
            Transmit Message via Contact Page →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </article>

  </div>
</Layout>
